  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Steganolide A and Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck, mediated through the CD81 antigen. Path_142051 indicates that Steganolide A targets the CD81 antigen, which in turn is a target of a compound named (1R,2S,5S,10S,14R,15R,21R)-1,2,8,8,15,20,20-heptamethyl-18-oxo-19-oxapentacyclo[12.9.0.02,11.05,10.015,21]tricos-11-ene-5-carboxylic acid, which is also a target of Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck. Path_142052 provides a direct link between Steganolide A and CD81 antigen, and then to Lck. The scores for both paths are relatively high, suggesting a plausible biological relationship. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where Steganolide A may modulate the activity of CD81, which in turn influences the activity of Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck. The relationship is supported by multiple evidence points, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
